t  this can then apply to climbing a tree  wrestling climbing a sheer cliff face  much better than simply performing these  same pull-up repetition over and over  again on a straight flat bar the same  thing goes for trail running versus  running now some of you might walk up  this idea and say that it's going to  lead to slower progress because you're  not practicing the exact right movement  pattern and this is true but it's a  trade-off that i think's more than worth  it this is what nikolai bernstein refers  to as repetition without repetition and  he says that this can lead to more  robust movement patterns norman deutsch  author of the brain that changes itself  he uses a great analogy and describes it  like tobogganing down the side of a  mountain you can either take the same  route down the side of the mountain  every single time and dig a deep trench  in the snow you'll be faster and quicker  down that mountain every single time  however if you want to take a slightly  different route it's going to be much  harder if you take a slightly different  route every single time you're going to  that way flatten out more of the snow  you're going to give yourself more  options for how you want to get down if  you want more options in the way you  move you need more varied movement  and now a word from this week's sponsor  morningbrew  so morningbrew is an email newsletter  that provides tech and business news in  an easily digestible manner  this is news that you'll actually read  and it will bring you up to speed with  events relevant to you prior to reading  morning brew over the last few weeks  most of the news i consumed was related  to the next sonic the hedgehog game  which some people would argue isn't  really news at all  now i get to feel more up to date and  grown up in conversation and it's  actually interesting and witty best of  all it only takes five minutes to read  just in the last few days i've been  following the 2022 olympics i read about  sony's