inging these kinds of  things around is fantastic at the same  time you get to feel like a badass you  look like the white wolf himself  swinging a metal club around your head  or you know you'll look like a complete  lunatic one or the other  if you want to take this even further  introduce even more vectors and  variables then you can also try using  predominantly what are called hybrid  exercises these are exercises that  combine two three even four exercises  movements in a single repetition so as  you're flowing from one movement  straight to the next before you repeat  the thing again an example of this would  be something like a devil press or a man  maker this is fantastic because not only  are you strengthening yourself in  multiple different positions not only  are you sending blood around the body by  training different parts of the body all  at the same time but at the same time  also strengthening the positions between  the movements these are the kind of  awkward angles the things we don't tend  to think of the transitions which is  often where we hurt ourselves in real  life so a fantastic example i'm going to  show you is the kettlebell cross body  clean and press one of my favorite  movements by far as it would happen  someone's left the kettlebell here  in the middle of the woods it's almost  like it was meant to be so  i can demonstrate  let's take my stuff out my pockets  this is an epic movement for a bunch of  reasons first of all you're combining in  here a kind of squat  slight hinge you've got to keep the back  nice and straight as you pick the weight  up off the ground at the same time  you're strengthening the core there's  even a bit of a pull for the lats and  the bicep as you get into that clean  position and there's a press you're  training the shoulders and the triceps  and the pecs to a lesser degree all in  one movement more importantly though  there's also a twist so you're engaging  the obliques and the quadratus lumborum  but it'